      {
        "type": "Module",
        "name": "usb_uart_bridge",
        "description": "CH340 USB-to-UART bridge interfaces the USB data pair to a UART channel and exposes the UART-side TXD and RXD signals for the board interface. This module consumes the generated VCC_3V3 rail and the external USB 5V rail per the provided pin set, with GND tied to the common ground. USB signaling enters on UD_P and UD_N from the external USB connector domain, while UART signaling leaves on TXD and enters on RXD toward the external target. The V3 pin is an additional CH340 supply-related node present in the provided pin list and should be treated as a local device support/configuration node during downstream wiring rather than a board-level exported rail. XI and XO indicate the device clock interface and require downstream implementation according to the selected CH340 operating topology; the provided component list does not include a clock source, so clock support remains a dependency to be resolved in later phases. Handshake/status pins CTS, DSR, RI, DCD, DTR, RTS, and mode-related R232 are present on the device but are not required by the brief, so they remain unexposed for the simple TXD/RXD-only interface unless later wiring assigns benign unused-state handling.",
        "id": "usb_uart_bridge"
